<p><strong>Author's Note: A Quick Note on Languages &amp; Gadgets in this Alternate Universe!</strong></p>

<p>Before we dive deeper into the chaos, here’s a quick guide to how everyone understands one another across different
    worlds:</p>
<ul>
    <li>This story may cross over with the gritty world of CID, with English‑dubbed cartoons like Pokémon and Beyblade,
        as well as 3D computer‑animated movies such as Barbie. All characters from those cartoon universes speak
        strictly in English, while our CID officers and local characters converse in Hindi.</li>
    <li>Wondering how they communicate without a language barrier or a common language? Ruhi, our
        brilliant original‑character gadgeteer, re‑engineered a Permanent Translation Jelly. Unlike temporary versions,
        her upgraded jelly makes its effects permanent. Once activated, anyone in Ruhi’s immediate vicinity is
        automatically synced to the translation matrix, allowing her to speak Hindi and be understood instantly,
        regardless of their native language.</li>
</ul>

